# Shop web config (VITE_*, build-time, NON-SECRET) — specs/007-shop-web/contracts/config.contract.md.
# Copy to .env.local and fill from the 001/004 SSM contract. NEVER commit real values.
#
# The SHOP pool — not back-office. Pasting the wrong pool id here makes sign-in succeed and every
# /shop/v1/* call return 401 from the shop authorizer, which looks like a bug in the backend.
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=   # ssm /effy/dev/auth/shop/user_pool_id
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=      # ssm /effy/dev/auth/shop/app_client_id
VITE_API_BASE_URL=           # ssm /effy/dev/edge/api_endpoint   (paths carry /shop/v1/...)

# Optional telemetry — degrades to a no-op when absent.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=

# ── Deployed (Amplify, 048-console-web-cicd) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# In the hosted dev build these VITE_* are supplied by Terraform (infra/envs/dev/amplify-consoles.tf)
# from in-account refs — no .env file, no operator step. All are PUBLIC-SAFE (a pool id, a client id,
# a gateway address); the console carries NO secret. Reference values for dev:
#   VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID = module.shop_pool.user_pool_id
#   VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID    = module.shop_pool.app_client_id
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL         = https://edge-api.dev.effyshopping.com   (paths carry /shop/v1/...)
# The console is served at https://shop.dev.effyshopping.com (its origin is CORS-allowed on the gateway).
